## Comprehensive Test Examples

@test_examples {
  "task_test": "@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)\nclass ArenaTaskTest {\n\n    @Mock\n    private EmulatorManager emuManager;\n    \n    @Mock\n    private Emulator emulator;\n    \n    @Mock\n    private DTOProfiles profile;\n    \n    @Mock\n    private NavigationHelper navigationHelper;\n    \n    @Mock\n    private StaminaHelper staminaHelper;\n    \n    private ArenaTask task;\n    \n    @BeforeEach\n    void setUp() {\n        when(profile.getEmulatorNumber()).thenReturn(\"0\");\n        when(emuManager.isRunning(\"0\")).thenReturn(true);\n        when(staminaHelper.hasEnoughStamina(20)).thenReturn(true);\n        task = new ArenaTask(profile, TpDailyTaskEnum.ARENA);\n        // Inject mocks via reflection or constructor if accessible\n    }\n    \n    @Test\n    void execute_EnoughStamina_CompletesSuccessfully() {\n        // Arrange\n        when(profile.getConfig(eq(EnumConfigurationKey.ARENA_TASK_BOOL), eq(Boolean.class)))\n            .thenReturn(true);\n        \n        // Act\n        task.execute();\n        \n        // Assert\n        verify(navigationHelper).navigateTo(\"ArenaScreen\");\n        verify(staminaHelper).hasEnoughStamina(20);\n    }\n    \n    @Test\n    void execute_InsufficientStamina_Reschedules() {\n        // Arrange\n        when(staminaHelper.hasEnoughStamina(20)).thenReturn(false);\n        \n        // Act\n        task.execute();\n        \n        // Assert\n        verify(staminaHelper).hasEnoughStamina(20);\n        // Verify rescheduling logic\n    }\n}",
  "service_test": "@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)\nclass ServProfilesTest {\n\n    @Mock\n    private IProfileRepository profileRepository;\n    \n    @Mock\n    private IConfigRepository configRepository;\n    \n    private ServProfiles service;\n    \n    @BeforeEach\n    void setUp() {\n        service = ServProfiles.getServices();\n        // Inject mocks\n    }\n    \n    @Test\n    void getProfiles_ReturnsAllProfiles() {\n        // Arrange\n        List<DTOProfiles> expectedProfiles = List.of(createTestProfile());\n        when(profileRepository.getProfiles()).thenReturn(expectedProfiles);\n        \n        // Act\n        List<DTOProfiles> result = service.getProfiles();\n        \n        // Assert\n        assertThat(result).isNotNull();\n        assertThat(result).hasSize(1);\n        verify(profileRepository).getProfiles();\n    }\n}",
  "helper_test": "@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)\nclass NavigationHelperTest {\n\n    @Mock\n    private EmulatorManager emuManager;\n    \n    @Mock\n    private Emulator emulator;\n    \n    @Mock\n    private DTOProfiles profile;\n    \n    private NavigationHelper helper;\n    \n    @Test\n    void navigateTo_ValidScreen_NavigatesSuccessfully() throws Exception {\n        // Arrange\n        when(profile.getEmulatorNumber()).thenReturn(\"0\");\n        when(emuManager.getEmulator(any(), any())).thenReturn(emulator);\n        helper = new NavigationHelper(emuManager, \"0\", profile);\n        \n        // Act\n        helper.navigateTo(\"AllianceScreen\");\n        \n        // Assert\n        verify(emulator).tap(eq(\"0\"), anyInt(), anyInt());\n    }\n}"
}

## Test Generation Requirements

When generating unit tests:

1. **Comprehensive Coverage**: Test all scenarios including valid inputs, invalid inputs, edge cases, boundary conditions, and exception scenarios (>80% coverage)
2. **AAA Pattern**: Structure all tests with clear Arrange, Act, Assert sections
3. **Proper Mocking**: Mock all dependencies (EmulatorManager, repositories, helpers, OCR providers) and verify interactions
4. **AssertJ Usage**: Use AssertJ for all assertions instead of JUnit assertions
5. **Naming Convention**: Follow [methodTested_ConditionTested_ExpectedResult] pattern
6. **Exception Testing**: Test exception scenarios (ADBConnectionException, HomeNotFoundException, OCR failures)
7. **Task Testing**: Test task execution, rescheduling logic, configuration access, helper usage
8. **Service Testing**: Test singleton access patterns, service methods, thread safety considerations
9. **Helper Testing**: Test helper methods with mocked dependencies, verify retry logic for OCR helpers
10. **Emulator Testing**: Test emulator operations with mocked ddmlib, verify caching behavior
11. **Repository Testing**: Test repository methods, HQL queries, use in-memory SQLite for integration tests
12. **Module Boundaries**: Respect module dependencies, test within module boundaries
